<wdkModel>

  <questionSet name="StrainSegmentQuestions" displayName="Strain Genomic Segments">

    <!-- Intentionally absent from Model/lib/wdk/ontology/individuals.txt so it does not
         appear in the category tree.  Still reachable by name via the service API: the
         same mechanism DynSpansBySegIds relies on (spanQuestions.xml:15, no
         individuals.txt row).  DynSpansByLocation is NOT a second precedent, despite
         looking like one: it exists only as an sqlQuery (queries/spanQueries.xml:266)
         with no question wrapping it and nothing consuming it across ApiCommonModel,
         ApiCommonWebsite, ApiCommonWebService, EbrcModelCommon or EbrcWebsiteCommon.  The
         only other mentions are the Model/vp2TuningTablesEffort inventories, where
         tableUsageMap.json records an EMPTY usage list for it, independently agreeing it
         has no users.  It is a dead id query, so it says nothing about service-API
         reachability.  Because
         nothing about categorization changes, `wb model` is the correct build target;
         `wb ontology` is not required.

         The queryRef below names the querySet 'StrainSegmentId', which follows the repo
         convention for id query sets (SpanId, GeneId, FileId).  It is unrelated to the
         Java class org.apidb.apicommon.model.report.bed.util.StrainSegmentId. -->
    <question name="StrainSegmentsByRefSegment"
              displayName="Strain Genomic Segment by Reference Location"
              shortDisplayName="Strain Segment"
              queryRef="StrainSegmentId.StrainSegmentsByRefSegment"
              recordClassRef="StrainSegmentRecordClasses.StrainSegmentRecordClass">

      <!-- summary lists every non-PK attribute the record class declares.  The BED
           download consumes a SUBSET of these: spec section 7's
           getRequiredAttributeNames(), in StrainSegmentFeatureProvider (added in
           ApiCommonWebsite a3c062e03), which declares four of them.  Notably strain and ref_seq
           are NOT consumed as attributes even though they are listed here, because the
           provider reads them out of the primary key.  Listing all of them beats an
           arbitrary subset, which would mean nothing to any consumer.

           NO sorting attribute, deliberately, and do not add one back because it looks
           harmless.  AnswerValue.prepareSortingSqls (AnswerValue.java:748..824) resolves
           a QueryColumnAttributeField's query and splices the whole attribute SQL into
           the ordering/paging statement, so sorting on any of these columns would re-run
           StrainSegmentAttributes.Coords, the apidb.indel prefix-sum aggregation, purely
           to order rows.  With no sorting declared, the fallback runs
           Question.getSortingAttributeMap (Question.java:669..681).  The question's own
           _defaultSortingMap is populated only from an attributesList sorting attribute
           (Question.java:759), so it is empty and line 680 delegates to
           RecordClass.getSortingAttributeMap (RecordClass.java:1441..1443), whose
           defaultSortingMap is likewise empty, so that falls back to the idAttribute, which is ordered
           against the id query alone and costs nothing.  Nothing is lost: strain_seq_id
           is a pure function of the primary key. -->
      <attributesList summary="organism,strain,ref_seq,ref_start,ref_end,strain_seq_id,strain_start,strain_end,strain_length"/>

      <summary>
        Given a genomic location in reference coordinates and a strain, return the
        equivalent segment in that strain's consensus sequence coordinates.
      </summary>

      <description>
        <![CDATA[
        Internal, webservice-only search. Takes a reference-coordinate genomic location
        (sequence ID, start, end, strand) plus a strain name, and returns the single
        equivalent segment in that strain's consensus sequence coordinates, shifted by
        the cumulative indel offsets recorded in apidb.indel. Intended to be consumed
        through the <em>bed</em> reporter for BED/FASTA download; it has no record page
        and no category-tree placement.
        ]]>
      </description>

    </question>

  </questionSet>

</wdkModel>
